    "body": "When we made the changes for the other controls i wondered briefly about password.  I didn't include it in the request because i thought of it as machine data, rather than readable text.  But on reflection, it is often possible to show the password in order to check it – in which case you'd probably want to have the right directionality applied if it contains a mix of RTL and other characters. Maybe that's mostly done client-side, but with a password manager perhaps there would indeed be situations where you'd want to retrieve a password from the server, and apply the appropriate directionality (which would involve dirname), so i suppose we should allow content authors to do that.\r\n\r\nThe same password, displayed in a RTL context, and a LTR context.\r\n<img width=\"197\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-09-01 at 13 43 42\" src=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/assets/4839211/5fdea057-a545-43bf-b6fa-aa1af16024ed\">\r\n\r\n<img width=\"206\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-09-01 at 13 43 28\" src=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/assets/4839211/a853a47f-232b-428b-b85b-2261006053e0\">\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
