    "created_at": "2023-10-09T17:09:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-09T17:09:06Z",
    "body": "Oh wait, I did think about the `button` element and it doesn't make sense there because what is shown to the user are the contents, but what is submitted to the server is the `value` attribute. That's very different from `<input type=submit>` where those are conflated. Supporting `<button dirname>` for the `value` attribute could be done, but that's different enough from `<input type=submit>` that I'm not sure it makes sense.",
